Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
You can specify "MUs to all successors", "MUs exiting independent of other MUs", or
"Main MU after other MUs".
Example
MyDismantleStation.Sequence := "Main MU after other MUs"
See also
Sequence [drop-down list] - DismantleStation
DismantleMode [SimTalk]
DismantleTable [SimTalk]
PickAndPlace Robot
PickAndPlace Robot
Use the object PickAndPlace robot for picking up a part at one station, rotating it, and placing it onto
another station.
Image
Description
The PickAndPlace robot can pick up and deliver one or more parts. To deliver several parts, type in the
Capacity. The PickAndPlace robot transports the part on to its successors within the flow of materials like
this:
• The part arrives at the exit of the predecessor. It notifies the PickAndPlace robot that it wants to be
picked up.
• The PickAndPlace robot then determines if it picks the part up or not.
◦ Without a Pull Control, the robot will be notified that a part wants to be picked up, and it accepts it.
◦ If you entered a Pull Control, the robot executes it, and when the part is selected, it will be picked up.
• The PickAndPlace robot rotates to the respective predecessor and picks the part up.
PickAndPlace Robot
11-1868 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• For determining the target station, the robot either uses its default Exit Strategies or the Target
Control. Within this Method you set the target station.
The Target Control is called, when the robot picks up a part or when it places a part. Within the method
setDestination the boolean parameter controls if the robot waits at the target station or not.
• Then, the PickAndPlace robot rotates to the target station and places the part.
• It then rotates back to the standard position.
The PickAndPlace robot can emulate most of the functions of the TransferStation.
To show a tooltip with information about the PickAndPlace robot, hover with the mouse over it.
Show Manipulators
To change the length of the graphic and the anchor points of the object, click Show Manipulators 
on the Edit ribbon tab or press M on the keyboard.
With the manipulators of the bounding box of the PickAndPlace-Robot you can edit its appearance of the
object.
PickAndPlace Robot
Plant Simulation Help 11-1869
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

With the rotation manipulator 
  you can set the rotation of the object with the mouse and with
keyboard keys:
Note
You cannot select a rotation manipulator together with anything else in a 3D window at the same time.
As soon as you select a rotation manipulator, Plant Simulation deselects the other selection.
As soon as you select anything else, Plant Simulation deselects the rotation manipulator.
This also applies when you hold down Ctrl or Shift when selecting.
• Drag the manipulator with the mouse to the right to rotate the object around the z-axis clockwise.
Drag the manipulator to the left to rotate the object counter-clockwise.
• Click the rotation manipulator and press the left arrow key or the right arrow key to rotate the object by
1° at a time.
Hold down Shift and press the left arrow key or the right arrow key to rotate the object by 45° at a time.
Add the Object to the Simulation Model
To add the object PickAndPlace robot to your simulation model, click 
  Manage Class Library > Basic
Objects > MaterialFlow > PickAndPlace on the Home ribbon tab.
Compare the sample models: Click the Window ribbon tab, click Start Page > Getting Started > Example
Models > Small Examples. Then, select the respective Category, the Topic, and the Example in the
dialog Examples Collection, and click Open Model.
