Six Axis Robot
Plant Simulation recognizes a robot as a six axis robot/6-axis robot if exactly the specified criteria are met.
• The first animatable object has a revolute joint around the rotation axis [0,0,1] or [0,0,-1] through the
rotation center [0,0,0].
Six Axis Robot
Plant Simulation Help 11-1875
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• And the first animatable object in the next lower level has a revolute joint around the rotation axis
[0,1,0] or [0,-1,0] through the rotation center [0,0,0].
• And the first animatable object in the next lower level has a revolute joint around the rotation axis
[0,1,0] or [0,-1,0] through the rotation center [0,0,0].
• And the first animatable object in the next lower level has a revolute joint around the rotation axis
[0,0,1], or [0,0,-1], or [1,0,0], or [-1,0,0] through the rotation center [0,0,0].
• And the first animatable object in the next lower level has a revolute joint around the rotation axis
[0,1,0] or [0,-1,0] through the rotation center [0,0,0].
• And the first animatable object in the next lower level has a revolute joint around the rotation axis
[0,0,1], or [0,0,-1],or [1,0,0], or [-1,0,0] (the latter two axes only apply if you also had [1,0,0], or
[-1,0,0] in axis number 4/the fourth bullet point in the list) through the rotation center [0,0,0].
• And the attribute _3D.AnimationObject exactly references the respective lowest animatable object.
• And a suitable animation path exists for the object, which the attribute _3D.AnimationObject
references.
Note
If any of the criteria listed above are not met, Plant Simulation will not recognize the object as a six axis
robot.
The six axis robot can reach all points in its gripping range. It can position the MU in all positions if it can
reach the position.
Note
If you change rotations of the three lowest-positioned animatable objects so that a rotation around a
slanting axis results, it might happen that the robot cannot position the MU in all positions even if it
is located within its gripping range. The same can occur if the toolholder of the robot is positioned
perpendicular above the insertion point.
If you change the rotation of any animatable object, except for the fourth object, so that the object is
rotated by an angle unequal to 0° around an axis that is not the rotation axis as specified above, it might
happen that the robot cannot position or rotate the MU as expected. The same might happen, if the
fourth object is rotated differently than either by an angle of -90° around [0,1,0] or by an angle of 90°
around [0,-1,0].
This also affects the pose/joint tool 
 , which might be positioned incorrectly.
Note
The six axis robot uses user-defined robot arm animations. If the robot does not have user-defined
robot arm animations, it moves up and down to make the animation look more realistic.
Six Axis Robot
11-1876 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Note
The robots PickAndPlaceComau.s3d and PickAndPlaceKuka.s3d in the installation folder > 3D > s3d-
graphics are six axis robots. You can replace a robot with these two robots with the command
Exchange Graphics.
