Four Axis Robot with Ball Joint Gripper
Plant Simulation recognizes a robot as a four axis robot with ball joint gripper/4-axis robot if exactly the
specified criteria are met.
• The first animatable object has a revolute joint around the z-axis through the coordinate [0,0,0].
• And the first animatable object in the next lower level has a revolute joint around the rotation axis
[0,1,0] or [0,-1,0] through the rotation center [0,0,0].
• And the first animatable object in the next lower level has a revolute joint around the rotation axis
[0,1,0] or [0,-1,0] through the rotation center [0,0,0].
• And the first animatable object in the next lower level has a revolute joint through the rotation center
[0,0,0].
• And the attribute _3D.AnimationObject exactly references the respective lowest animatable object.
• And a suitable animation path exists for the object, which the attribute _3D.AnimationObject
references.
Note
If any of the criteria listed above are not met, Plant Simulation will not recognize the object as a four
axis robot with ball joint gripper.
The four axis robot can reach all points within its gripping range. It can position the MU in all positions if it
can reach the point.
Note
If you change the rotation of any animatable object, except for the fourth object, so that the object is
rotated by an angle unequal to 0° around an axis that is not the rotation axis as specified above, it might
happen that the robot cannot position or rotate the MU as expected.
This also affects the pose/joint tool 
 , which might be positioned incorrectly.
Note
This robot uses user-defined robot arm animations. If the robot does not have user-defined robot arm
animations, it moves up and down to make the animation look more realistic.
Four Axis Robot with Ball Joint Gripper
Plant Simulation Help 11-1881
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Note
The default robot in Plant Simulation is a four axis robot with ball joint gripper. You cannot move its
poses and joints with the mouse or with keyboard keys.
