SCARA Robot with Concluding Prismatic Joint
Plant Simulation recognizes a robot as a SCARA robot with concluding prismatic joint if exactly the
specified criteria are met.
• The first animatable object has a revolute joint around the rotation axis [0,0,1] or [0,0,-1] through the
rotation center [0,0,0].
• And the first animatable object in the next lower hierarchy level has a revolute joint around the
rotation axis [0,0,1] or [0,0,-1] through the rotation center [0,0,0].
• And the first animatable object in the next lower hierarchy level has a revolute joint around the
rotation axis [0,0,1] or [0,0,-1] through the rotation center [0,0,0].
• And the first animatable object in the next lower hierarchy level has a prismatic joint with the
translation direction [0,0,1] or [0,0,-1].
• And the attribute _3D.AnimationObject exactly references the respective lowest animatable object.
• And a suitable animation path exists for the object, which the attribute _3D.AnimationObject
references.
Note
If any of the criteria listed above are not met, Plant Simulation will not recognize the object as a SCARA
robot with concluding prismatic joint.
The SCARA robot with concluding prismatic joint can reach all points within its gripping range. It can
only place the MUs in positions which are exclusively described by a rotation around the z-axis.
Note
If you change the rotation of any animatable object that is a revolute joint, so that the object is rotated
by an angle unequal to 0° around an axis that is not the rotation axis as specified above, it might
happen that the robot cannot position or rotate the MU as expected.
This also affects the pose/joint tool 
 , which might be positioned incorrectly.
Note
The robot PickAndPlaceComauSCARA.s3d in the installation folder > 3D > s3d-graphics is a SCARA
