Loading Time [PickAndPlace]
The Loading Time is the time it takes the PickAndPlace robot for picking up a part at a station. If the
PickAndPlace robot is full, it rotates to the target station and places the part there.
Remarks
The Loading Time is the time it takes the PickAndPlace robot for picking up a part at a station.
• If the delivering station is a point-oriented object, the part is booked on the PickAndPlace robot while it
picks it up. The delivering station is locked until the loading time has elapsed.
• If the delivering station is a length-oriented object, the part remains on the delivering station during the
loading time and is then moved on to the PickAndPlace robot.
Select a distribution, and type the values, which that distribution requires, into the text box. Plant
Simulation shows these values along the upper border of the tab.
You can also enter a constant time (Const).
If you select the Formula distribution, you can type in a numeric expression or the name of a Method.
You can use the anonymous identifier @ to access the part for which the loading time applies. The
anonymous identifier ? points to the PickAndPlace robot.
Note
During the Loading Time no part can be placed onto the delivering station.
Note
Behavior during interruptions of the PickAndPlace robot
Plant Simulation extends the Loading Time by Interruption times of the PickAndPlace robot. The
delivering station remains locked during the interruption.
Note
Behavior during interruptions of the delivering station.
Loading Time [PickAndPlace]
11-1904 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Interruptions of the delivering station do not affect loading the part by the PickAndPlace robot. The
loading operation will be executed while the interruption lasts.
Note
The entrance of the PickAndPlace robot is open while its Loading Time is running. The entrance is
closed once the part is actually moved on. The PickAndPlace robot opens the entrance again after the
Unloading Time has passed.
SimTalk
LoadingTime [SimTalk] - PickAndPlace
LoadingTime.Type [SimTalk] - distribution parameter
IsLoading [SimTalk]
putAttributeNamesIntoTable [SimTalk] - distributions
Loading Time [PickAndPlace]
Plant Simulation Help 11-1905
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Unloading Time [PickAndPlace]
The Unloading Time is the time it takes the PickAndPlace robot for placing the part it picked up at another
station onto the target station.
Remarks
The Unloading Time is the time it takes the PickAndPlace robot for placing the part, which it picked up at
another station, onto the target station.
• If the target station is a point-oriented object, the part is booked on the PickAndPlace robot while it
places it. The target station is locked until the unloading time has elapsed.
• If the target station is a length-oriented object, the part is moved on to the length-oriented object before
the Unloading Time starts.
Select a distribution, and type the values, which that distribution requires, into the text box. Plant
Simulation shows these values along the upper border of the tab.
You can also type in a constant time (Const).
If you select the Formula distribution, you can type in a numeric expression or the name of a Method.
You can use the anonymous identifier @ to access the part for which the unloading time applies. The
anonymous identifier ? points to the PickAndPlace robot.
Note
Behavior during interruptions of the PickAndPlace robot.
Plant Simulation extends the Unloading Time by interruption times of the PickAndPlace robot. The
target processing station remains locked during the Interruption.
Note
Behavior during interruptions of the target station.
Interruptions of the target station do not affect unloading the part by the PickAndPlace robot. The
unloading operation continues while the interruption lasts.
Unloading Time [PickAndPlace]
11-1906 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Note
The entrance of the PickAndPlace robot is open while its Loading Time is running. The entrance is
closed once the part is actually moved on. The PickAndPlace robot opens the entrance again after the
Unloading Time has passed.
