Wait for Free Target [PickAndPlace]
To only rotate the PickAndPlace robot to a part that wants to exit the predecessor and to pick it up if the
destination object is also ready to receive it, select this check box.
Remarks
To rotate the PickAndPlace robot immediately to the part, clear the check box.
Activating Wait for Free Target prevents that the PickAndPlace robot transports parts to a Station or a
Conveyor that is already occupied or reserved. The PickAndPlace robot thus is available for other jobs that it
can do the moment.
Plant Simulation only evaluates Wait for Free Target for the setting Target Selection > Exit strategy or
target control.
Plant Simulation enters the part that cannot be transported into the Forward Blocking List of the target
object.
Note
If you select the check box, Plant Simulation already evaluates the entered Exit Strategy or the Target
Control for the part before the PickAndPlace robot rotates to the part to pick it up.
Plant Simulation enters the thus determined target into the text box Target Object.
